{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-96808",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{4,5,8,9,10,12,13\\},$ and the set $S=\\{4,5,8,9,10,12,13\\}$ has $|S|=7$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}, & x=4,5,8,9,10,12,13 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $6$ items $(5,8,9,10,12,13)$ that satisfy $X\\ge 5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 5)=6\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{6}{7}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
